#basePath P2_Outreach_Note
#include "Header.leaf"

:: Start
@exposed
@trigger    OnLocationChanged
// "NONE" ensures no other threads are in-progress
// global:currentPhase == 2 ensures player is in phase 2
@when       global:currentThread == "NONE", global:currentPhase == 2, location == "ArmyCorps"
@cutscene
// Lock all location on map
$call SetInThreadLocks()
$call DisableMapButton()

$call  ClearVisibleLines()

// Mark start of thread
$set global:currentThread = "P2_Outreach_Note"
$call SetBackground("bg/army-corps-bg.png")


{@}   
       You park your car on the side of the road, the Army Corps of Engineers building up ahead.
       In it's shade, you have a sudden memory of being here for a high school field trip. 
       At the time, Janie had said she could see herself in the Corps. You find her number quickly on your phone and call her.

{@You}
       Hey Janie! Random question, but do you remember when we visited the Army Corps of Engineers in high school?

{@Janie}
       <i>Yeah, I guess.</i>

{@You}
       Think you'd ever wanna come back?

{@Janie}
       <i>Probably not. Why would I want to go back to the middle of nowhere?</i>

{@You}
       I'm back in the middle of nowhere.

{@Janie}
       <i>Ana, come on, you know what I mean. Look, I gotta go. I'll call you later, okay?</i>

{@}
       The call disconnects. You sit for a moment in your car, gnawing at your lip, before stepping out. 
       An engineer working on a trap notices you and waves. You wave back.

{@You}
       Hello. Sorry to interrupt, but could I ask you some questions? 

{@}
       The engineer stands up and nods warmly. You notice the surname "Robertson" embroidered on their high-visibility vest. 

{@Robertson}
       Yes, of course. Thanks for stopping by. 

{@You}
       I had some questions about sea lamprey management. You were pretty involved in previous management efforts, right?

{@Robertson}
       Yes, ma'am. We were very involved. We built traps, barriers, helped coordinate lampricide application. The whole works.

{@You}
       And these were successful?

{@Robertson}
       Yes, ma'am, they were. We helped reduce the population by 90%. Nothin' if not efficient. //receive evidence chip
       Hasn't been so much work done lately, but we're always ready to restart. 
       $call GiveEvidenceChip("Evidence-awareness-program")

{@You}
       Well, I'm creating an intervention plan for managing sea lamprey populations. Have any advice?

{@Robertson}
       'Course I do, ma'am. All those things I mentioned earlier - barriers, traps, the like - restarting 'em will help. 
       In the meantime, though, getting the locals onboard will help lots. 
       If they can tell us where they are seeing bites, that can help us identify tributaries to target. 

{@You}
       That can be done. I know some people down at the docks. 

{@Robertson}
       Well, don't be a stranger, ma'am. Come back when you want yer traps. 

{@You}
       Don't worry. I will. 

{@}
       By the time you get back to your car, your previous phone call is almost forgotten. 

// Give evidence chip

// skip to end
$goto .End


:: End
@exposed
@tracked
// Mark end of thread
$set global:currentThread = "NONE"

// Go to Phase 2 Continue Hub
$goto P2_Hub.Continue